Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||02-20-2000||04:45 AM||||Well it started of good I was coming home from school 9were I just had 4 tests.  I was coming home thinking that me and my friends were going to head out to temple academy dragway (texas) an get some times, especially for my car.  Well turns out someone screwed up the dates and there was no racing.  So friday we go out to the local cruising spot and as I was getting on it pretty hard comiung out of a parking lot turning left I hear pop reeeeeee(thats my motor shooting way up to the red line)  Then I hear clunk, clunk, clunk.  Turns out it was the passenger cv shaft was down by the controll arm.  that was at 12 by the time AAA got me home it wass 3:30.  My dad gets me up at 8 and hes has to go work at the go- kart track.  I take it appart and doesn't look like it hit the tie rod or anything but there was cv grease an needle bearings everywhere!!!! [major negative]  after my dad gets back it turns out we have the parts to make another shaft (mine requires an inner to fit the 4t60e and the outer to fit into the spindle).  So my dads having the axle rebuilt at a local shop on monday.[+]  I am gona catch a ride back to school with a friend so thats a [plus]. After that we took my friends out to the go-kart track where they got a whole new appreciation of 70 mph, point is on the way to the track I saw a what appeared to be a really good condition yellow formula and the guys had the hood up, I wished I could have stopeed but we were trying to get to the kart track.[++]  so sisne my car was out of comission I was with my frinds and we went out to our normal spot in the sticks to do some racing.  Well my friend with an ls1 t/a and another guy with a ls1 z are about to go then we hold of cause a car is coming, turns out its a county mounty, he checked all the cars for "beer" and everyone was clean so he let us go with a "I never want to catch ya'll out here again", wheeee was that a relief,[+} because if my fiero hadn't broke the night before I might have ben out there racing. [another plus!], I guess the moral of this rambling story is that from now on the fiero will be used only for transportation to and from school, the karting season starts soon so I can get the racing out of my system that way![++]but for<BR>the time being no more hotrodding, cause the next axle that breaks is coming out of my pocket{-}.  I also have ben seing alott of fieros lately.  which leads me to my only question I saw what I think was an se and it looked like it had some ribbed body panells/ground effects.  the looked aftermarket but maybee stock???? point is I have never seen one like that before & would like to know what it was.  <BR>anyways thats my story and I am sticking to it!||||reg||4
